breaking_changes.Adaptation_method:
Remove all uses of `onFID()` and corresponding imports from your code. There is no direct API replacement for this metric in the current release. For example:

// Before:
import { onFID } from 'web-vitals';
onFID(callback);

// After:
// No direct replacement. Remove these lines entirely.

If your code compares or groups attribution selectors as strings, ensure you allow for (or explicitly sort) class names in selectors. For example, if previous output was 'div.a.b.c' and it could now be 'div.a.b.c' regardless of input order, you do not need to change code. But if your downstream code stored and expected 'div.c.b.a', update logic as follows:
// Before (order not guaranteed)
const sel = attrib['attribution selectors']; // could be 'div.c.b.a'
// After (order always guaranteed lexicographically)
const sel = attrib['attribution selectors']; // always 'div.a.b.c'
// If comparing old data, sort or migrate old attribution selectors to canonical order for consistent grouping.
